 was  told to read the prequel very  specifically at this point in the series  which i can only assume means that the  information within it is going to be  important for the very next arc which i  imagine means that utah is going to  appear because other than him not  another whole lot really happened here  that we're not aware of in the series as  it stands after hidden inventory or well  actually i suppose a ghetto's family  could also be important his whole gang  of sorcerific  peeps two of which were the little girls  from his flashback which was a nice  tie-in but utah and those characters  aside i don't think anything  majorly important happens that we didn't  already know so i'm bracing myself for  the return of our former protagonist and  wondering how his sorcery has evolved  without the use of rika although my  biggest question mark actually comes  from the idea that this prequel series  is being made into a jujutsu kaisen  movie which seems like quite a brilliant  move there's just enough material in  here to make a satisfying feature and  given that it is effectively an isolated  story you could feasibly walk into it  without having seen  or read jujutsu kaisen itself i'm  curious to see what changes they will  make though specifically  maybe to characters like ghetto and gojo  because this is one of those situations  where crafting a faithful adaptation to  the source material probably  won't actually do those characters  justice because they've both just  evolved so much since this short series  but as for the ultimate question of when  you should read the prequel  this might just be my bias because this  is the way i did it but i don't think  it's ideal to start with it's a fun  series of chapters to look back on with  a greater context of what jiu-jitsu  kaisen has become i just think that  nakatami does such a superior job of  introducing the world and its characters  in the sequel series so starting at that  high  is what i would prefer the first 